---
import core from '../../../lib/relational-collection/core.json';
const rows=[...core.orders,{order_id:105,customer_id:1,placed_at:'2026-10-21T12:00:00Z',status:'pending'},{order_id:106,customer_id:3,placed_at:'2026-10-21T12:00:00Z',status:'pending'}];
---
<figure class="key-figure" data-key-order data-rows={JSON.stringify(rows)} aria-labelledby="r10-key-title">
 <figcaption id="r10-key-title"><span>Figure 2</span> Which entries must the search pass?</figcaption>
 <p class="question">Customer 1’s two newest orders since 15 October:<br/><code>ORDER BY placed_at DESC, order_id DESC LIMIT 2</code></p>
 <label>Index key <select data-key><option value="customer">Customer only</option><option value="history" selected>Customer, then newest</option><option value="date">Newest across customers</option></select></label><p class="key-code" data-key-label data-live></p>
 <div class="key-layout"><div><p class="panel-label">Index entries in key order</p><ol data-entries></ol></div><div class="answer"><p class="panel-label">Answer · newest first</p><ol data-answer></ol><p data-count data-live></p></div></div>
 <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 2 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>Read this comparison as text</summary><p>The customer-only index finds 101, 103 and 105, then dates must be checked in the table and the qualifying rows sorted. The history key starts at customer 1’s newest entry and reads 105, then 103; both qualify and LIMIT stops it. The date-first key reads 106, 105 and 103 to find those same two orders. Order 106 belongs to Edda, so the scan passes it.</p></details>
 <p class="caption">A conceptual entry walk over the core orders plus the later illustrative orders 105 and 106. It does not predict a native plan for five rows. Both later orders are pending; this changes no receipt or payment in the core report.</p>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-key-order]').forEach(root=>{
 const rows=JSON.parse(root.dataset.rows!);const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-key]')!;
 const displayDate=(value:string)=>new Date(value).toLocaleDateString('en-GB',{day:'numeric',month:'short',timeZone:'UTC'});
 const qualifies=(r:any)=>r.customer_id===1&&r.placed_at>='2026-10-15';
 const sorted=()=>[...rows].sort(select.value==='customer'?((a,b)=>a.customer_id-b.customer_id||a.order_id-b.order_id):select.value==='history'?((a,b)=>a.customer_id-b.customer_id||b.placed_at.localeCompare(a.placed_at)||b.order_id-a.order_id):((a,b)=>b.placed_at.localeCompare(a.placed_at)||b.order_id-a.order_id));
 const visited=()=>select.value==='customer'?sorted().filter(x=>x.customer_id===1):select.value==='history'?sorted().filter(x=>x.customer_id===1).slice(0,2):sorted().slice(0,3);
 const draw=(step:number)=>{root.querySelector('[data-key-label]')!.textContent=({customer:'(customer_id)',history:'(customer_id, placed_at DESC, order_id DESC)',date:'(placed_at DESC, order_id DESC, customer_id)'})[select.value];const path=visited();const seen=path.slice(0,step);const complete=step===path.length;const answer=seen.filter(qualifies).sort((a,b)=>b.placed_at.localeCompare(a.placed_at)||b.order_id-a.order_id).slice(0,2);
 root.querySelector('[data-entries]')!.innerHTML=sorted().map(r=>`<li class="${seen.includes(r)?'read':''}"><strong>${r.customer_id}</strong><span>${displayDate(r.placed_at)} · order ${r.order_id}</span><small>${seen.some(x=>x.order_id===r.order_id)?'read':''}</small></li>`).join('');
 // Rows are re-sorted objects; compare identities for styling.
 root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-entries] li').forEach((el,i)=>el.classList.toggle('read',seen.some(x=>x.order_id===sorted()[i].order_id)));
 root.querySelector('[data-answer]')!.innerHTML=(select.value==='customer'&&!complete?[]:answer).map(r=>`<li>Order ${r.order_id} · ${displayDate(r.placed_at)}</li>`).join('');
 root.querySelector('[data-count]')!.textContent=`${seen.length} entries read${complete&&select.value==='customer'?'; 3 table rows checked; sort needed':complete?'; stop at 2 matches; no sort':''}`;
 root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=step===0?(select.value==='customer'?'Find customer 1. These entries do not tell us each order’s date.':select.value==='history'?'Find customer 1’s newest entry. Its date and order ID already give the requested order.':'Start at the newest entry across all customers.'):complete?(select.value==='customer'?'101 is too old. Check all three rows, then sort 105 ahead of 103.':select.value==='history'?'105 and 103 qualify. No later entry can displace them, so the scan stops.':'Pass 106 because it belongs to customer 3. Then 105 and 103 complete the answer.'):`Read order ${path[step-1].order_id}${qualifies(path[step-1])?' — it qualifies.':' — it does not qualify.'}`;
 };
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>visited().length+1,draw});select.addEventListener('change',()=>{player.render();root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-reset]')!.click();});
 });
</script>
<style>
 .key-figure{padding:1rem;margin:2rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);font:.9rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.2rem var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:1rem}figcaption span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.7rem}.question{font-size:.9rem}.key-code{font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-mono);overflow-wrap:anywhere}.key-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.4fr 1fr;gap:1.25rem;margin:1rem 0}.panel-label{font-weight:600}ol{list-style:none;padding:0}.key-figure :global(li){display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;padding:.6rem;margin:.4rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface)}.key-figure :global(li small){margin-left:auto;color:var(--color-accent)}.key-figure :global(li.read){outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:-2px}.answer{min-height:10rem}select{display:block;max-width:100%;font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);padding:.5rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);margin-top:.4rem}.controls{display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}button{font:inherit;padding:.45rem .65rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);border-radius:.25rem;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);cursor:pointer}button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.5}button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}[data-explanation]{min-height:4.5em;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.8rem}[data-hold]{height:3px;width:100%;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{height:100%;display:block;background:var(--color-accent);width:0}.caption{font-size:.82rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}details{margin-top:1rem}summary{cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:520px){.key-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}.answer{min-height:0}select{font-size:.8rem}}
</style>
